<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        Deliberately updatable, and deliberately not only a post_init_hook.

        A hook fires on install alone, so a database built before a fix in the
        builder keeps the broken data for ever. That is exactly what happened to
        the supplier pricing, whose company was wrong on every one of the 33
        rows. build_all() is idempotent by construction, so running it again on
        upgrade is a no-op that also repairs drift.
    -->
    <function model="alshayeb.demo.builder" name="build_all"/>

    <!--
        Document A §14: eighteen months of history, and §13's seeded conditions.

        This call is the whole difference between a database that looks like a
        company and one that looks like a fresh install. It was missing: the
        generator existed from Session 7 and nothing ever invoked it, so every
        installed database had zero manufacturing orders, zero sales orders,
        zero invoices, zero quality checks, and fourteen of the eighteen
        conditions in §13, including every security condition but one, simply
        were not there.

        Volume is reduced and shape is not: both Ramadans, both Hajj seasons,
        the Hijri drift, the seasonal curve, the lot genealogy and every seeded
        condition are present. The trial build is capped at 1 GB, and §14's
        literal row counts do not fit inside it. See DEVIATIONS.md.

        Idempotent per record, like the builder above, so an upgrade re-runs it
        as a no-op that fills in whatever a previous version did not create.
    -->
    <function model="alshayeb.demo.history" name="generate_default"/>
</odoo>
